\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Invariant mass spectra of MC in the (a) $\omega (782)$, (b) $\phi (1020)$, and (c) $\omega ^{\prime }/\omega ^{\prime \prime }$ mass regions. The distributions correspond to $M(pK_S^0)$, $M(p\pi ^0)$, and $M(K_S^0\pi ^0)$, respectively. The "Truth-Matched" distribution (green dashed line) corresponds to reconstructed events where the momentum directions of the $\pi ^0$ and $\gamma _{\mathrm  {ISR}}$ successfully match their truth-level counterparts. A loose requirement of $\chi ^2_{\text  {KF}} < 100$ is applied to the kinematic fit. The continuous spectrum of $\sqrt  {s'}$ for the $\pi ^+\pi ^-\pi ^0$ system demonstrates the radiative return mechanism via ISR. \relax }}{8}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:signal_mc_mass_spectra}{{1}{8}{Invariant mass spectra of MC in the (a) $\omega (782)$, (b) $\phi (1020)$, and (c) $\omega ^{\prime }/\omega ^{\prime \prime }$ mass regions. The distributions correspond to $M(pK_S^0)$, $M(p\pi ^0)$, and $M(K_S^0\pi ^0)$, respectively. The "Truth-Matched" distribution (green dashed line) corresponds to reconstructed events where the momentum directions of the $\pi ^0$ and $\gamma _{\mathrm {ISR}}$ successfully match their truth-level counterparts. A loose requirement of $\chi ^2_{\text {KF}} < 100$ is applied to the kinematic fit. The continuous spectrum of $\sqrt {s'}$ for the $\pi ^+\pi ^-\pi ^0$ system demonstrates the radiative return mechanism via ISR. \relax }{figure.caption.6}{}}
